From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:23:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 142/144] GreatDANE: tighten NSIS continuation joining and stop
 pre-deleting sentinels (round 4m)

Treat a trailing backslash as a continuation only after stripping ASCII
space, tab, and CR. Refuse any line that contains NUL, a C0 control
other than tab, or non-ASCII whitespace. Add H1 (comment backslash plus
NBSP) and H8 (NUL before the backslash) fixtures; their /tmp sentinels
must not be created.

Try $DANE_ESR_MOZBUILD first when importing the preprocessor, then
sys.path, then the boxed ESR tree. FAIL if a command sentinel already
exists before a run, and do not delete it.
